auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Ex-Libris API

  A self-hosted book tracker. All /books routes require authentication; /healthz
  is open.

  ## Auth
  Every book request sends `Authorization: Bearer {{token}}` (inherited from this
  collection).

  - **Local dev** (`AUTH_DISABLED=true`): the token is ignored — a static `dev`
    user is used — so requests work with whatever `token` the environment holds.
  - **Real OIDC** (Authelia): put a valid JWT access token in the environment's
    `token` variable.

  ## Flow
  Run "Create Book" first — it saves the new id into the `bookId` environment
  variable, which "Get / Update / Delete Book" then reuse.
}
